ing to happen  that's such an egregious case and that's  why it's not that big of a deal unless  the agent wants to make it a big deal  because they want to get a win for  themselves and for their agency  meanwhile the player suffers clearly the  team suffers because Donald it's going  to be their face as a franchise they  hope for the next decade I just think  that you have to keep in mind that the  agent works for the player and a lot of  times in this industry in this business  players defer to their agents especially  young players and ie players rookie  players and and that's why this isn't  about Sam Donald the CAA is also  representing role Quan Smith and I think  the AAA is in the right for holding  outro kwan smith because he is a  linebacker and the Bears are looking to  void guaranteed money if he's suspended  for an illegal hit and with this new  lowering helmet rule that's much more  applicable to a linebacker so I  understand the agency's position in that  case but that's not applicable for Sam  darlin and if Sam Donald flunks or fails  a steroid test and I think he should  have some of his guaranteed money voided  so I don't have an issue with the team's  stance in that case I just believe in  this particular instance the agent is  not doing right by his client and  because of that his client is suffering  the team is suffering and ultimately  depending on how long this lasts  it could affect whether Sam Donald will  be there week 1 starter because they  certainly want to give him every  opportunity over the next 5 weeks to do  that yeah that was what I was gonna  bring up Manish and that is the  likelihood that Sam darn 'old is the  starting quarterback for the Jets and  you're saying that they're holding out  hope or they're preparing for that I  don't want to put words in your mouth  but how would you describe that  situation well they wanted to evaluate  him in a vacuum you've also got Teddy  Bridgewater and Josh McCown of course  and you know the